Reject split counts of 0, and -b counts too large for off_t.
The -b count was parsed as unsigned long long and stored in an off_t,
so one above the off_t maximum became negative: split then wrote empty
or partial pieces and could loop forever. A count of 0, for -b or -l,
was accepted: -b 0 created empty pieces until the names ran out, and
-l 0 put all the input in one piece. Parse both counts in the range 1
to the off_t maximum, which settles both problems in the same lines.

---
 coreutils/split.c |    6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/coreutils/split.c
+++ b/coreutils/split.c
@@ -113,9 +113,9 @@
 	);
 
 	if (opt & SPLIT_OPT_l)
-		cnt = XATOOFF(count_p);
-	if (opt & SPLIT_OPT_b) // FIXME: also needs XATOOFF
-		cnt = xatoull_sfx(count_p,
+		cnt = xatoull_range(count_p, 1, OFF_T_MAX);
+	if (opt & SPLIT_OPT_b)
+		cnt = xatoull_range_sfx(count_p, 1, OFF_T_MAX,
 				IF_FEATURE_SPLIT_FANCY(split_suffixes)
 				IF_NOT_FEATURE_SPLIT_FANCY(km_suffixes)
 		);
